================================================================================
REGULATORY & COMPLIANCE STATEMENTS (EU AI ACT / FERPA / INDIA DPDP ACT)
================================================================================

1. European Union Artificial Intelligence Act (EU AI Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689):
   - SSIF algorithms and risk models fall under Annex III, Paragraph 3 (Education
     and Vocational Training: systems intended to be used to evaluate learning
     outcomes, assess student admissions, or predict academic performance/retention).
   - In accordance with Article 14 (Human Oversight), SSIF predictions and algorithmic
     recourse recommendations are strictly decision-support advisory instruments.
     Fully automated negative determinations, student dismissals, or disciplinary actions
     without human academic counseling review are strictly prohibited.

2. Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA, 20 U.S.C. § 1232g):
   - Re-identification risk mitigation: Small-cell metric suppression is enforced across
     all experiment and reporting modules. Any subgroup or profile with sample size
     n < 5 suppresses aggregated continuous statistics to prevent singling out individual
     student trajectories.

3. India Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDP Act, 2023):
   - All dataset interactions honor purpose specification and data minimization principles.
   - Cross-cohort merges without cryptographic pseudonym linkage are explicitly rejected
     by automated architectural compatibility gates (RULE-002).
